  "steps": [
    {
      "id": "s01",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "By the end of this tutorial, a requirements document already in your Confluence will have become test cases on a branch in your repository.",
      "minHoldSeconds": 1.5,
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-01.png",
          "caption": "Open the Confluence tab",
          "focus": {
            "x": 0.134,
            "y": 0.2702
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s02",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Velox works from a document you have already written, not a blank template.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-02.png",
          "caption": "Your existing Confluence pages"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s03",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Select the document you want tested. Generate Test Scenarios turns live beside the Jira and Confluence actions.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-02.png",
          "caption": "Select the document to test",
          "atWord": 0,
          "focus": {
            "x": 0.2991,
            "y": 0.5265
          }
        },
        {
          "screenshot": "step-03.png",
          "caption": "Generate Test Scenarios turns live",
          "atWord": 6,
          "focus": {
            "x": 0.8609,
            "y": 0.1955
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s04",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Press it, and the scenario document opens, naming the BRD it came from and the scope it covers.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-04.png",
          "caption": "Overview, scope, and source BRD"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s05",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Each scenario carries an objective, the preconditions it assumes, and the happy path written as numbered steps.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-05.png",
          "caption": "Objective, preconditions, happy path"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s06",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "It also lists edge cases and negative cases, which is the part a story on its own never carries.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-05.png",
          "caption": "Edge and negative cases listed"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s07",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Push the document to Confluence, and it becomes a page your team can review and the Testing tab can read.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-05.png",
          "caption": "Push the document to Confluence",
          "atWord": 0,
          "focus": {
            "x": 0.885,
            "y": 0.1061
          }
        },
        {
          "screenshot": "step-06.png",
          "caption": "Page created in Confluence",
          "atWord": 5
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s08",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Open the Testing tab, which is where those scenarios turn into test cases.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-07.png",
          "caption": "Open the Testing tab",
          "focus": {
            "x": 0.1295,
            "y": 0.5155
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s09",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Velox opens by asking how your IDE will send test cases back, because your IDE is what writes them.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-08.png",
          "caption": "Your IDE writes the test cases"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s10",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "With the MCP server connected, your IDE chains the whole flow and the results arrive here on their own.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-08.png",
          "caption": "MCP connected, results arrive here"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s11",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Without it you copy the prompt out and paste the results back. That is the path this video takes.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-08.png",
          "caption": "Manual copy and paste path",
          "focus": {
            "x": 0.6785,
            "y": 0.7219
          }
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s12",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Manual mode is two steps. Pick a scenario page, then deliver what your IDE gives you.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-09.png",
          "caption": "Two steps, pick then deliver"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "s13",
      "role": "body",
      "narration": "Open the page list, and Velox marks which of your pages actually hold scenarios.",
      "beats": [
        {
          "screenshot": "step-09.png",
          "caption": "Open the page list",
          "atWord": 0,
